# the ewe desktop (pulls the full DE: Hyprland, Quickshell, Komble, ewe-settings, …)
ewe
# explicit so pacstrap settles the libjack provider up front — otherwise a
# dependency's 'jack' requirement auto-picks jack2, which then conflicts with
# the pipewire-jack that ewe's own dependency tree brings in
pipewire-jack
# explicit for the same reason: zed wants a `vulkan-driver`, and unclaimed pacman
# picks nvidia-utils (1 GB, and it blacklists nouveau — the live session then had
# no GPU driver on NVIDIA, which is why nvidia-open used to ride along). Mesa's
# CPU Vulkan claims it; nouveau / i915 / xe / amdgpu drive the live desktop.
vulkan-swrast
